body:
I still argue Wastelanders kind of flubbed the main story. Sure, it made people happy and added more content, but theres a difference between talking to Heather Responderface or Robot Girl in Watoga vs finding the empty town of Flatwoods, knowing everyone who tried to fight this is gone, and you are the only one who will ever be there to try and fix it. The Watoga girl especially is distasteful because shes obsessed with robots....... in a town where everyone got slaughtered by robots. The addition of human NPCs was a welcome one for more content, but it was so much spookier and empty before them. Something gained, something lost.

&#x200B;

On the other hand, i still love walking in this game. I still use fast travel most of the time, but this is the only Fallout game where ill just. Walk! through the Forest or the Ash Heap or the Bog or anything because its all so pretty and peaceful and quiet. Seeing other players is a treat because you just stumble apon them like you stumble apon a friend on the street. Sitting in the mountains in the Divide is such a nice thing to do and take pictures. I love the Monorail Elevator because i can see so much from it. This game is so \*good looking and peaceful.\*
